      "text": [
        " سَمِعْتُ أَبَا عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) يَقُولُ إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ عَيَّرَ أَقْوَاماً بِالْإِذَاعَةِ فِي قَوْلِهِ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ وَ إِذا جاءَهُمْ أَمْرٌ مِنَ الْأَمْنِ أَوِ الْخَوْفِ أَذاعُوا بِهِ فَإِيَّاكُمْ وَ الْإِذَاعَةَ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "A number of our companions, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad Bin Khalid, from Usman Bin Isa, from Muhammad Bin Ajlan who said, ",
          "‘I heard Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> saying: ‘Allah<sup>azwj</sup> Mighty and Majestic has Blamed a people for the publicising in the Words of the Mighty and Majestic <span class=\"ibTxt\"><a href=\"/#/books/quran:4#h83\"><a href=\"/books/quran:4#h83\">[4:83]</a></a> And when there comes to them news of security or fear they publicise it</span>. Therefore beware of the publicising’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "1. A number of our people have narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Khalid from ‘Uthman ibn ‘Isa from Muhammad ibn ‘Ajlan who has said the following: “I heard abu ‘Abd Allah (a.s.) saying, ‘Allah, the Most Majestic, the Most Holy, has criticized people for publicizing confidential matters in His words, “When they receive any news of peace or war, they announce it in public. . . <a href=\"/#/books/quran:4#h83\"><a href=\"/books/quran:4#h83\">[4:83]</a></a> Therefore, be on your guard against publicity of confidential matters.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
